    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32866" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏpūs</span></b> ,
		ūntis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀποῦς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Locris</i>, <i>in
			Greece</i>, now <i>Kardhenitza</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 28,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 1, 3, 73</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏpūn-tĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Opuntian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 3, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7, 12, § 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Philodamus,</span>”
				<i>of Opus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 44, § 109</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏpūntĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Opus</i>, <i>the
			Opuntians</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 28, 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
